      "text": "8 December saw US President Ronald Reagan and Soviet General Secretary Mikhail Gorbachev sign the historic **INF Treaty** (Intermediate-Range Nuclear Forces Treaty) during a momentous superpower summit in Washington D.C. The groundbreaking accord mandated the complete elimination of an entire category of land-based nuclear and conventional cruise missiles, initiating unprecedented on-site inspection protocols on both sides of the Iron Curtain. Reagan famously deployed the Russian proverb \"trust, but verify\", to which a grinning Gorbachev dryly replied that he heard it repeated at every single meeting.",
