      "text": "7 December saw a catastrophic magnitude 6.8 earthquake strike northern **Armenia** in the Soviet Union, devastating the cities of Spitak, Leninakan and Kirovakan. Poorly reinforced concrete apartment blocks collapsed instantly, killing an estimated 25,000 to 50,000 people and leaving half a million homeless in freezing winter conditions. In an unprecedented move that underscored his policy of *glasnost*, Soviet leader Mikhail Gorbachev cut short a state visit to the United Nations in New York and formally accepted search-and-rescue assistance from Western nations for the first time since World War II.",
