      "text": "3 October saw astrophysicists publish decisive orbital measurements demonstrating the presence of a supermassive **black hole** at the centre of our galaxy, **Sagittarius A***. By tracking the astonishing velocities of nearby stars orbiting the Milky Way's core, researchers proved that millions of solar masses were concentrated in an extraordinarily compact cosmic region. The landmark discovery provided conclusive proof for long-debated gravitational theories, eventually yielding the 2020 Nobel Prize in Physics.",
