      "text": "7 June saw Dublin teen pop quartet **B*Witched** leap straight to number one on the UK singles chart with their infectious debut *C'est la Vie*. Sporting matching head-to-toe double denim and executing lightning-fast traditional Irish step-dancing, the four singers unleashed a relentless pop hurricane of tin whistles and cheerful innuendo. The track instantly took up permanent residence inside the heads of British school pupils, making denim waistcoats an inescapable summer uniform.",
