      "text": "16 October saw former Chilean military dictator **Augusto Pinochet** arrested by British police while recovering from back surgery at a private clinic in London. Acting on an international extradition warrant issued by crusading Spanish magistrate Baltasar Garzón regarding the torture and disappearance of Spanish citizens, the arrest shattered the traditional assumption that former heads of state enjoyed permanent immunity for crimes against humanity. British legal circles erupted into fierce constitutional debate, while elderly Chilean exiles danced with joy in Trafalgar Square.",
